    "display_name": "Recommend a Game",
    "long_instructions": "You are building a decision tree classifier to help recommend games to your friend. You have a dataset in `games.csv` with information about your friend and the games they like and dislike.\r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:**\r\n\r\n1. Look at `games.csv` and decide which columns are the features of your dataset. Fill in the names of those columns in the `feature_names` list in `main.py`. \r\n2. Look at `games.csv` and decide which column is the label for your dataset. Fill in the name of that column in the definition of `outputs` in `main.py`. \r\n3. Create a new model using `DecisionTreeClassifier`.\r\n4. Fit your model to the training data with the `fit` method.\r\n5. Score your model on the test data. You can use the `score` method on a model to score it on test inputs and outputs.\r\n6. When you’re done, run your program and look at the visualization of the decision tree your program learned. What did your decision tree learn? You’ll answer a question about this in the next level.\r\n\r\nIf you get stuck, you can ask AI Tutor for help with the structure of your program!",
